# Every worker image is built with server/ as the context (docker-compose.yml,
# docker-compose-integration-tests.yml, workers/build_docker_images.sh), so this is
# the file Docker reads for all of them. It keeps local working-tree state out of
# the images: caches, notebooks, editor and R session files, local renv projects,
# and local secrets and env files. A build from a clean checkout is unaffected.

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
**/.cache
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/*.ipynb

# R and RStudio. The image's renv project is created by the build, not copied.
**/renv
**/.Rprofile
**/.Rhistory
**/.RData
**/.Rproj.user
**/*.Rproj

# Local secrets and environment files
**/.orcidtoken.json
**/*.env
workers/certs

# Tests, test data and coverage output. Tests run from the working tree or from a
# mounted volume (docker-compose-integration-tests.yml), not from the images.
**/tests
**/test
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.py
**/conftest.py
**/pytest.ini
**/requirements-dev.txt
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml

# Other local files
**/.DS_Store
**/*.bkp
workers/base/output
